T*
(The UI is intentionally static and simple. It demonstrates the API without adding a) Tj
T*
(separate frontend framework or build step.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SOLID PRINCIPLES) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY PRINCIPLE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Each major class has one primary responsibility:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `GameOfLifeEngine` calculates board states.) Tj
T*
(- `BoardValidator` validates and parses board inputs.) Tj
T*
(- `JsonBoardStore` handles JSON file persistence.) Tj
T*
(- `Program.cs` wires HTTP endpoints to services.) Tj
T*
(- `BoardStateResponse` represents output data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This keeps the code easier to test and reason about.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(OPEN/CLOSED PRINCIPLE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The persistence layer is behind `IBoardStore`. The API can be extended with another) Tj
T*
(storage option, such as SQLite, Postgres, or cloud storage, without rewriting the) Tj
T*
(endpoint logic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For example, a future `SqlBoardStore` could implement `IBoardStore` and be registered in) Tj
T*
(dependency injection.) Tj
ET
